  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Indian Poker (Forehead Poker). Setup: 2-8 players, 52-card deck. Deal: one card per player, face-down. Players hold cards to forehead without looking. Gameplay: Standard poker betting. Players see all cards except their own. Highest single card wins pot. If player folds or only one remains, winner takes pot. In showdown, simple card ranking: A high down to 2 low.',
    Player: "Indian Poker: Each player gets one card held to their forehead. You see everyone else's cards but not yours. Bet based on what you see others holding. Highest card wins the pot. If you see many high cards, fold. If mostly low cards, call or raise.",
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest card (or convincing others you do) when players showdown, or by being the only player not to fold.',
    gameplay: "1. Each player is dealt one card face down\n2. Without looking at their card, players hold it to their forehead so all other players can see it\n3. Players look around at all other players' cards\n4. A round of betting occurs (similar to poker)\n5. Players can fold, call, or raise based on what they see\n6. After betting, remaining players showdown\n7. The player with the highest card wins the pot\n8. If multiple players tie for highest, they split the pot",
    keyRules: [
      'Players must NOT look at their own card(s)',
      'All players can see all cards except their own',
      'Standard poker betting rules apply',
      'Highest card wins in single-card version',
      'Players may fold if they believe their card is low',
      'Bluffing is based on betting patterns, not card hiding',
    ],
